{"context":"Workers cover discussion, execution and review. EKA is removing ownership, so roles cannot live in the EKA store as assignments. A role config that becomes the only source of truth would be a second, ungoverned SoT.","decision":"Worker roles (discuss, implement, review) are steward-controlled configuration binding role -\u003e ACP driver -\u003e prompt template. The config is versioned, schema'd and code-reviewed. Roles select driver and template ONLY — never work selection (work selection is code-owned ordering, see the determinism ADR). Roles never touch EKA and never decide control flow. Independent review is code-enforced, distinct from the author role where configured.","consequences":"Roles evolve with steward config, not the EKA store; EKA stays model-agnostic and intentionally loses ownership queryability (a deliberate, recorded consequence of the solo-author ADR). Review independence and config validity are code-enforced and tested.","alternativesConsidered":"Store roles in EKA as member/assignment artifacts (rejected: re-introduces ownership). Hard-code roles (rejected: inflexible). A single generic worker (rejected: no independent review). Free-form role config (rejected: ungoverned SoT)."}